const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"为什么单看收益不够",en:"Why expected return is not enough"},body:{zh:"Markowitz把选择过程分成形成未来判断与据此配置资产两步，本文研究后一步。若只追求最高预期收益，很难解释为何要分散持有；文章因此把预期收益与收益方差一起纳入选择。这里讨论的是给定判断后的取舍，不是如何预测股票。",en:"Markowitz separates forming beliefs from choosing a portfolio given those beliefs. The paper addresses the second task. Maximizing expected return alone cannot explain a preference for diversification, so variance enters alongside expected return. It is a framework for choices conditional on beliefs, not a stock-forecasting procedure."}},{title:{zh:"材料是模型，不是回测样本",en:"A model, not a backtest sample"},body:{zh:"输入是各证券的预期收益、方差和两两协方差，以及由投资者确定的权重。本文所展示的推导排除负权重，且权重之和为1。它没有给出某一市场或某段历史的优胜组合；历史收益只是后来估计这些输入的一种可能材料。",en:"Inputs are expected returns, variances, pairwise covariances and investor-chosen weights. The displayed analysis excludes negative weights and requires weights to sum to one. It does not report a winning historical portfolio. Using past returns to estimate its inputs is an additional empirical choice."},reference:{url:"https://www2.stat.duke.edu/courses/Fall07/sta103/markowitz.pdf",label:{zh:"原文：组合收益与方差定义",en:"Original: portfolio return and variance definitions"}}},{title:{zh:"关键一步：把共同变动算进去",en:"The key step: include co-movement"},body:{zh:"组合期望收益是个别期望收益的加权和；组合方差还包含证券之间的协方差。因此，给两只各自波动很大的证券配权，结果取决于它们是否一起涨跌。只比较单只证券的风险，或者只数持仓个数，都会漏掉组合层面的关系。",en:"Portfolio mean is a weighted sum of individual means; portfolio variance also includes cross-security covariance terms. Combining two volatile securities therefore depends on their co-movement. Ranking securities by stand-alone volatility, or counting holdings, misses this portfolio-level relationship."}},{title:{zh:"有效集合说明了什么",en:"What the efficient set tells us"},body:{zh:"文章用几何方式描述可达到的收益—方差组合。在预期收益相同或更高时方差最低，或者方差相同或更低时期望收益最高的组合，构成有效选择的边界。这不是唯一答案：投资者仍需在边界上选择自己愿意接受的风险与收益组合。",en:"The geometric argument describes attainable mean–variance combinations and their efficient boundary. Efficiency means that another feasible portfolio cannot improve the relevant mean–variance trade-off. It does not identify one universally best allocation: the investor must still choose a preferred point on that boundary."},reference:{url:"https://www2.stat.duke.edu/courses/Fall07/sta103/markowitz.pdf",label:{zh:"原文：有效集合与几何说明",en:"Original: efficient-set and geometric discussion"}}},{title:{zh:"阅读时先分清三个对象",en:"Keep three objects separate"},body:{zh:"建议依次区分个别证券的随机收益、事先固定的持仓权重，以及由两者组合得到的收益分布。读协方差式子时，检查非对角项如何改变结果；读有效边界时，再问哪些权重被允许。更换约束或预期判断，就已经在研究另一个可行集合。",en:"Track random security returns, fixed allocation weights and the resulting portfolio distribution separately. In the variance expression, inspect the off-diagonal terms; in the efficient-set argument, inspect the allowed weights. Different constraints or beliefs define a different feasible problem."}},{title:{zh:"把模型带入数据前",en:"Before bringing data to the model"},body:{zh:"编辑建议：先冻结收益定义、证券范围、观察窗口和缺失处理，再讨论估计。协方差矩阵所用的日期必须对齐，不能让不同证券在不同样本上悄悄计算。估计误差、交易成本与现实约束需另行处理；一条画出来的边界不能证明未来表现。",en:"Editorial application: freeze return definitions, the universe, observation windows and missingness rules before estimation. Align covariance inputs to a defensible common sample. Estimation error, trading costs and real constraints need separate treatment; a plotted frontier does not validate future performance."}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文建立的是给定预期与协方差后的选择框架；样本估计、偏好和现实约束改变时，结果也会改变。",en:"This is a conditional choice framework. Estimated inputs, preferences and real-world constraints can change the result."}};export{e as default};
